sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 (a task group is one root task; Pi turns use the pi driver), Recall swamp-tasks-swamp-orchestrates-pi + task-vms-swamp-via-ssh, DECISIONS R1-R4.
  %% Tightened: flow-tighten 2026-11-02, rule 22. Cut 2026-11-02 (orchestrator): provision creates the VM and the workspace only; the group-run driver composes tasks.check, tasks.turn, tasks.publish, tasks.park and tasks.cancel, each with its own receipt, key and budget.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: tasks:provision
  %% kind: tasks.provision
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane VM icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane H icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant VM as Task VM<br/>tvm-88 over ssh
  participant H as Incus host<br/>Node 14 · VM power
  CLI->>GW: tasks:provision 42<br/>--idempotency-key=KEY
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit tasks:provision 42 --idempotency-key=feature.42`
  %%> - syntax: `<group> [--idempotency-key=KEY] [--json]`
  %%> Input:
  %%> - the task group id; the group already holds its subtasks and deliverables
  %%> Who can call it:
  %%> - the `orbit` CLI and the MCP tool `tasks-provision` send the same request; the group-run driver calls it first for a `todo` group
  %%> After it:
  %%> - the driver runs `tasks:check`, `tasks:turn`, `tasks:publish`, `tasks:park` and `tasks:cancel`, each as its own task with its own receipt, key and budget
  Note over GW: Validate, record the task<br/>group 42: reserved · task #5140
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - your Node has Gateway access, and the Tasks extension is on
  %%> - group 42 is `todo`, external, and every subtask has a deliverable
  %%> - no other task holds `task_group:42`
  %%> Capacity:
  %%> - the Gateway picks a host with room and the promoted image of the current recipe, for example Node 14
  %%> Image fallback:
  %%> - while a host builds the current recipe, or after that build failed, it serves the host's last promoted image if that image was promoted at most one day ago
  %%> - a group created with `current_recipe: true` never takes a fallback image; it waits for the current recipe, as before
  %%> - with no current image and no fallback under a day old, the task waits (`waiting`, reason `capacity`) until a build promotes
  %%> - with no room, the task waits (`waiting`, reason `capacity`); the Gateway starts it when a task VM is destroyed or an image is promoted
  %%> Result:
  %%> - task #5140 recorded with the full intent: Project, repository, branch `task-42`, the start commit and the setup steps
  %%> - VM 88 reserved on Node 14, and the workspace Instance recorded
  %%> - VM 88 records the image it got: recipe identity, fingerprint, image build, and whether it is a fallback
  GW->>SW: Push the VM secrets<br/>vault: model key, Pi token
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - writes the secrets for VM 88 into the Swamp vault: its model key, its Pi token, the provider bootstrap and, for a private repository, the Git read authorization
  %%> Why:
  %%> - secrets go Gateway → vault → step; the run inputs hold only vault key names
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-task-provision
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - starts one Swamp run on serve (Node 209)
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - the group, VM 88 and Node 14, the workspace and the Project setup steps
  %%> - the SSH identity comes from the `swamp` role; task VMs run no Swamp worker
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task #5140
  %%> What you get:
  %%> - the task number, at once
  %%> Next:
  %%> - follow it with `operation:show`, and the board with `tasks:show 42`
  SW->>H: Create and prepare the VM<br/>launch · WireGuard · Pi server
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - creates VM 88 from the promoted recipe image, with the read-only package cache mounted
  %%> - joins VM 88 to WireGuard with its own hub peer file, pins its SSH host key, and starts the Pi server, then checks Pi answers
  %%> Per provider:
  %%> - Incus: `incus launch` on Node 14 over SSH, then one bounded wait until the guest agent answers
  %%> - UpCloud overflow: the UpCloud API from 209, with the token from the vault
  %%> How:
  %%> - the shared task VM workflow, the same one `task_vm.provision` runs
  SW->>VM: Set up the workspace<br/>clone · Project setup steps
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - builds the workspace connection from the host key the VM step pinned
  %%> - clones the repository on 209 and copies it as a Git bundle, on branch `task-42` from the start commit
  %%> - reads the checkout with one `@swamp/ssh exec` argv each: `identity` (HEAD and branch), `analysis_base` (merge base with the default branch) and `inspect` (`stat` of `composer.json` and the entry point)
  %%> - `composer` downloads a regular `composer.json` with one `@swamp/ssh copy` into the private worker directory, so its text never reaches native history
  %%> - `profile` on 209 refuses a checkout on another commit, classifies the source and keeps the start commit's merge base as the fixed analysis base; it reads and deletes the downloaded `composer.json` and keeps only its PHP version and Laravel flag
  %%> - runs the Project setup steps in order as `setup-0`, `setup-1`, …: each is one `@swamp/ssh exec` argv in the checkout, with its own timeout; each writes its output to a file on the VM, and only a redacted 4 KiB tail reaches history
  %%> - for the proof Project only, writes the proof club key as a 0600 file from SSH stdin
  %%> - no step copies a script to the VM
  Note over SW: Check the workspace<br/>receipt · VM, source, base
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - reports one receipt: the VM's readiness, the source and the analysis base, or the first failed step and its error code
  %%> - a failed VM or workspace step has already failed the run; this step only reports
  alt every step passes
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event; Swamp never calls the Gateway
    Note over GW: Record result<br/>group 42 running · VM 88 ready
    %%> Result:
    %%> - VM 88 is `ready` with its `tvm-88` Node; the workspace Instance is `source_resolved` on the start commit
    %%> - group 42 is `running`; task #5140 succeeds with the starting commit, the analysis base and the image VM 88 got (`image.recipe_identity`, `image.fingerprint`, `image.build_id`, `image.fallback`)
  else a step fails
    VM--xSW: exit ≠ 0 or timeout
    %%> When:
    %%> - a create, enrollment, clone, setup or proof key step fails, or the budget ends
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
    %%> The Gateway reads:
    %%> - the receipt: which step failed, its error code, and whether VM 88 got ready
    Note over GW: Mark the task failed<br/>group asks for help
    %%> Result:
    %%> - task #5140 fails; a VM that got ready is recorded, and the Instance keeps the failed step
    %%> On the VM:
    %%> - VM 88 and its checkout stay; there is no rollback
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - `tasks:cancel 42` ends the group and removes the VM
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show #5140
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - asks for the task's status every 2 seconds until it has ended
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the current status, and the result once the task has ended
  end
